On 03-Mar-93 in The Dungeon Gourmet (food &..
user Ward C. Burrows@ugcs.cal writes:
>"You feel healthy." - poison resistance.
>Any poisonous insect or snake, cave spiders, brown or black puddings, gray
>oozes, shriekers, green dragons (always), unicorns.  Warning:  poisonous
>monsters leave poisonous corpses!
 
Nope, not always.  Cave spiders are nice because they do not create
poisonous corpses, nor do shriekers.  Also, I believe all of the molds
will give you poison resistance on occasion, and only yellow molds are
poisonous (although yellow and violet are both hallucinagenic).
 
>"You feel wide awake." - sleep resistance.
>Elves (any type), orange dragons (always), homunculi, possibly acid blobs?
>(acid blobs are an unverified rumor...)
 
Consider it confirmed.  Sir Loin of Beef (my latest try with a Knight)
just got sleep resistance from an acid blob, as well as poison
resistance from a shrieker.
 
>"You feel full of hot air." - cold resistance.
>Blue jellies, winter wolves, yetis, white dragons (always), possibly anything
 
>else with a cold-based attack, brown or black puddings.
 
Brown mold.
 
>"You feel a momentary chill." - fire resistance.
>Red molds, red dragons (always), brown or black puddings, possibly anything
>else with a fiery attack (like hell hounds).
 
>"Yum.  That was real brain food!  You feel smart!" - +1 INT.
>Mind flayer.  These always give you something:  intrinsic telepathy if you
>don't already have it, extra INT if you do!
 
Nope, they don't always give you something.  I was playing a barbarian
who already had telepathy, and he noshed a mind flayer and didn't get
diddly.  I also believe he scarfed one when he lost telepathy (am I the
only one who thinks it is stupid that offing the High Priest of Moloch
(or any sub-priests) causes you to lose telepathy?  c'mon, we don't have
any choice!) and didn't get anything.
 
>(no message) - loss of intrinsics!
>gremlins?  (unconfirmed)
 
There is a message:  "The gremlin chuckles."  Then it gives you a second
message corresponding to what intrinsic got swiped (i.e. "You feel warm"
corresponds to a loss of fire resistance).  Real pain in the butt, I
tell ya, especially when a gremlin finds some water and multiplies
itself.
 
